/* SpbSelfHelp - SELF-BRAIN (2026-10-03): the offline helper understands the app and the buyer's current situation.
   Owner: "people will never feel stuck or frustrated not knowing how to do whatever they may want to their paint schemes."
     SpbSelfHelp.state()              what is loaded right now (nothing / flat paint / PSD + layers), zones, selected zone, car map, Pro vs Easy, last action
     SpbSelfHelp.classify(text)       help intent: how_do_i / what_is / where_is / why_not / stuck / can_i / explain_state (null = not a help question: never claims an order)
     SpbSelfHelp.answer(text, state)  {intent, text, steps, cites, next, doIt} - numbered steps naming the exact control and where it is, adapted to the state
     SpbSelfHelp.diagnose(state, q)   why-not checks against the state (no zone selected, muted, colour mode, covered by a higher zone, stale preview ...)
     SpbSelfHelp.chips(state)         state-aware starter chips [[label, say], ...]
     SpbSelfHelp.redirect(text)       a chip label that is really another brain's order -> the phrase that brain understands
     SpbSelfHelp.runDoIt(text)        a "Do it: ..." chip -> performs the safe, reversible action it promised (select / unmute a zone, refresh the preview)
   ES5, no DOM at load time, every app read wrapped: node tests pass a fake state (_easy_claude_work/selfhelp_test.js).
   Data: UI_DATA (controls, generated by _easy_claude_work/selfhelp_build.py from scripts/ai_atlas/app_controls.json + ui_map.json) + TOPICS (goals) below. Docs: docs/SELF_HELP.md. */
